        "combat": false,
        "source": "The Four Types of Injuries",
        "description": "<h3 id=\"the-four-types-of-injuries\"><em>The Four Types of Injuries</em></h3>\n<p>Earlier, we discussed the three categories of injuries, but there are different ways of getting injured. There are four types of injuries in Titan World, blunt injuries, cutting injuries, piercing/ballistic injuries, and burning injuries. If a character is injured in any other way, use your own discretion.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align:center;\">Cut</th>\n<th style=\"text-align:left;\">When a cut is a minor injury, any rolls on cutting attacks towards the same limb have advantage, for each existing cut. When a cut is a major injury, you will steadily lose points of consciousness, at the GM’s discretion. Bleeding will have a cap of however many major cut wounds are present. At 1-4 wounds, there is a cap of -1 consciousness from bleeding, and at 5, you can die from bleeding. When a cut is a crippling injury, that limb is completely severed. Crippling cuts can also deal lethal bleeding. A crippling cutting wound to the head is an instant death.</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Blunt</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">When you receive a minor blunt wound, any rolls on blunt attacks towards the same limb have advantage, for each existing bruise or fracture. When a blunt wound is a major injury, the bone is considered to be broken, and must be set with a splint or cast to be treated. When a blunt wound is a crippling injury on one of the 4 limbs, that limb’s bone is completely shattered, and must be amputated. When a blunt wound is a crippling injury on the chest, you receive a spinal injury, and are crippled from the waist down. When a blunt wound is a crippling injury on the head, you receive permanent brain damage, reducing your “Mind” stat to -3, which cannot be raised any higher.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Piercing (Ballistic)</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">When a piercing injury is a minor injury, it has the same stat check debuffs as a major injury. When a piercing injury is a major injury, the wound bleeds similar to a major cutting injury. When a piercing injury is a crippling injury, it either completely shatters a bone beyond repair, or destroys an organ inside the body. A crippling piercing wound to the head will instantly kill the target, and a major wound will blast a hole through their jaw in some way, preventing them from speaking.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center;\"><strong>Burn</strong></td>\n<td style=\"text-align:left;\">When a burn is a minor injury, any rolls against being burned are difficult, for each existing burn. Three minor burn wounds will automatically become a major wound. When a burn is a major injury, you must pass a <strong>Roll+Body</strong> or begin to bleed. When a burn is a crippling injury, the limb is completely charred and dehydrated, and essentially unusable. It must be amputated to function. A crippling burn  wound to the chest or head is untreatable, and will result in a slow and certain death.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>",
