        "difficult": false,
        "combat": true,
        "source": "Surviving a Titan’s Grasp",
        "description": "<h3 id=\"surviving-a-titan’s-grasp\"><em>Surviving a Titan’s Grasp</em></h3>\n<p>When encountering a Titan, they’ll often try to grab the nearest human. If they’re outside of your hand-to-hand size range, they’ll simply pick you up. Of course, this can be avoided with a good enough <strong>Roll + Agility</strong>. However, after a successful roll to dodge away from a Titan, you’ll receive a -1 to each subsequent Agility check until you can catch your breath.  <br />\n There are two ways to go about trying to escape a Titan’s grasp, pure strength, or slicing yourself free. If you’re skilled enough with your blades, and have a free hand, you can make a difficult <strong>Roll + Technique</strong> to slice open the Titan’s hand, and escape free. If that’s not an option, you can make a difficult <strong>Roll + Body</strong> to try to pry yourself out of the Titan’s grasp, though this takes long enough that your gear will be destroyed by the time you’ve made your way out, crushed by the Titan’s grasp. While in a Titan’s grasp, it is important for the GM to remember that a roll of 6 or lower is a failure in which the player must find a new approach to roll again. This means that the player <em>cannot</em> just continuously roll until they are free after failing.</p>",
