        "key": "hang-on-to-a-stuck-blade",
        "stat": "body",
        "category": "Titan hunting",
        "difficult": false,
        "combat": true,
        "source": "Killing Titans Without Maneuver Gear",
        "description": "<h4 id=\"killing-titans-without-maneuver-gear\"><strong><em>Killing Titans Without Maneuver Gear</em></strong></h4>\n<p>You probably won’t be able to. Killing a Titan without manoeuvre gear follows the same rules as normal, except for two key differences. The first one is that you cannot slice chunks out of a Titan, due to lacking the momentum, and the second is that only a titan-slaying blade can pierce its skin. The eyes and ears are still susceptible to guns and knives, if you can reach them.  <br />\nIf you’ve managed to make your way to a Titan’s weak point, you must succeed in a difficult <strong>Roll + Technique</strong> to get your titan-slaying blade into the right spot, a difficult <strong>Roll + Body</strong> to actually force it to move in the way you want, and then a difficult <strong>Roll + Agility</strong> to successfully slice out a chunk of it faster than it can regenerate. If you fail any of these rolls, you fall off of the Titan, and your blade is stuck inside of its nape. You may <strong>Roll + Body</strong> to try and hang on. On a 7-9, you can retain the hilt, but the blade snaps off, and on a 10+, you manage to keep your grip. You must make this roll again every time the Titan moves, and must <strong>Roll + Body</strong> if you wish to take your sword out. On a 10+, you get the sword out, and on a 7-9, the blade snaps.  <br />\nAlternatively, you can blow up a Titan’s weak spot with a cannon or explosive, which would kill it.</p>",
