        "combat": false,
        "source": "Fear",
        "description": "<h2 id=\"fear\">Fear</h2>\n<p>The world of Attack on Titan is a scary place. When seeing a Titan for the very first time, seeing a Titan eat a comrade (every time), or anything else that would completely shake a man’s soul, <strong>Roll + Heart</strong>. On a 7-9, your next roll is difficult. On a 6 or lower, you are completely frozen in fear, until you’re snapped out of it. If you roll a 9 or lower when seeing a Titan for the first time, you must <strong>Roll + Heart</strong> every time you see a Titan until you roll a 10+.  <br />\nWhen snapping a comrade out of a state of fear, <strong>Roll + Duty</strong>. On a 10+, the player is completely recovered, and can act again. On a 7-9, they can follow you and act somewhat, but will automatically fail any roll until they have a minute to rest, in which case they will snap out of it. On a 6 or lower, you fail completely and someone else has to try, or they must be brought somewhere completely safe and had roughly a half hour (or equivalent) to calm down.  <br />\nWhen instilling fear into the heart of an NPC, <strong>Roll + Duty</strong>. On a 10+, the NPC is completely frightened, and will do as commanded. On a 7-9, they’re afraid, but might lash back, and might hesitate to follow orders. On a 6 or lower, either you completely failed to frighten someone, or you’ve frightened them so much that they see the situation as having no choice but to attack you, at the GM’s discretion.</p>",
