        "description": "<h3 id=\"fighting-dirty\"><em>Fighting Dirty</em></h3>\n<p>When fighting an opponent, we can’t expect everyone to play fair. When performing a dirty trick to catch someone off-guard, like attacking when someone isn’t expecting it, or throwing sand in their eyes, your opponent must <strong>Roll + Mind</strong>. On a 7-9, you gain a <strong>+1 Advantage</strong> to your next attack roll. On a 6 or lower, you gain a <strong>+2 Advantage</strong>.  <br />\nWhen performing a dirty trick to cause more pain than expected, such as kicking your opponent in the testicles, roll your attack as normal. Then, if it connects, your opponent must <strong>Roll + Heart</strong>. If your body or technique (depending on the attack) is a +2  or higher, this roll is considered difficult. On a 7-9, your opponent loses an extra point of consciousness immediately. On a 6 or lower, your opponent loses a point of consciousness, and is prone. This does not stack, however, so you can’t just smash someone’s nuts continuously to stop them from ever acting.</p>",
