        "key": "wrestle",
        "stat": "body",
        "category": "Combat",
        "difficult": false,
        "combat": true,
        "source": "Wrestling",
        "description": "<h3 id=\"wrestling\"><em>Wrestling</em></h3>\n<p>When wrestling an opponent, both fighters must <strong>Roll + Body</strong>. The one with the lower roll is pinned to the ground, grappled, or otherwise unable to move, until he wins another roll contest of Body. On a 10+ from the defender while still lower than your opponent’s Body roll, you are still pinned to the ground, but can still punch your opponent, or hit them in a similar manner. You can also use a weapon, if you have access to one. These attacks can be dodged or blocked as normal.  <br />\nWhen wrestling, you may also choose to strangle your opponent. This follows the general suffocation rules until you stop or your opponent breaks free.  <br />\nWhen attacking an opponent, after your hit has landed, you can choose to <strong>Roll + Technique</strong> or <strong>Roll + Body</strong> to try and throw them to the ground. On a 10+, you can wrestle your opponent starting with the upper hand (having them pinned to the ground, unable to act), or choose to stand where you are. If you choose to stand where you are, your opponent will lose consciousness equal to their own body stat. On a 9 or lower, you fail to properly throw your opponent, and both of you fall to the ground. This can be done on any attack, including a counterattack.</p>",
