        "difficult": false,
        "combat": true,
        "source": "Being Prone",
        "description": "<h3 id=\"being-prone\"><em>Being Prone</em></h3>\n<p>When you are prone on the ground, you must <strong>Roll + Body</strong> to stand. If you are below half of your maximum consciousness, you must <strong>Roll + Heart</strong> as well, and pass both rolls. On a 10+, you manage to stand with no issues, and on a 7-9, your next roll is considered difficult. Whoever rolls the highest Agility is able to act first. If one person is prone, and the opponent is not, then the person on the ground has a chance to roll to stand up before the opponent can act, but the opponent gets a free action once that roll has been made.</p>",
