        "key": "mount-a-horse",
        "stat": "duty",
        "category": "Soldier duties",
        "difficult": false,
        "combat": false,
        "source": "Riding Horses",
        "description": "<h2 id=\"riding-horses\">Riding Horses</h2>\n<p>They say a dog is a man’s best friend, but a dog won’t carry you for miles on end, under the harsh sun. The horse is the soldier’s greatest means of transportation aside from the 3D Maneuver Gear itself, but it’s equally as challenging to get proper use of.  <br />\nWhen getting on a horse, <strong>Roll + Duty</strong>. On a failure, you can’t get the horse to obey you, and it’s frightened in some way. Every following check on this horse will be difficult, until you can calm it down with a difficult <strong>Roll + Duty</strong> check.  <br />\nWhile riding a horse, you may <strong>Roll + Duty</strong> to perform a difficult manoeuvre in some way. This could be speeding beyond your horse’s usual running speed, or weaving between various obstacles.  <br />\nWhen dismounting your horse, <strong>Roll + Agility</strong>. On a failure, you fail to dismount gracefully, and fall onto the ground. Your next roll will be difficult.</p>",
