        "category": "Soldier duties",
        "difficult": false,
        "combat": false,
        "source": "Firing Cannons",
        "description": "<h2 id=\"firing-cannons\">Firing Cannons</h2>\n<p>Loading, aiming, and firing a cannon in total requires three actions. First, you must load your ammunition. On a regular black powder cannon, this can be done without a roll. On more advanced artillery, <strong>Roll + Duty</strong>. Then, you must aim the cannon. This requires a <strong>Roll + Mind</strong>. Following this, <strong>Roll + Technique</strong> to properly fire it while keeping the aim steady.  <br />\nThroughout this, each action takes up a “turn” in the sense that whoever you’re going against can act after each action. If your target moves after you’ve aimed, you must aim again.  <br />\nMultiple people can cooperate to fire a cannon, this means that with three people, you can load, aim, and fire all on the same “turn”, giving your opponent no chance to react.  <br />\nIf a Titan is hit with a cannon, a limb of the aimer’s choice is incapacitated. If the aimer chooses to, they can call to aim for the nape, but this must be done before they or the firer rolls. If the aimer or the firer rolls a 9 or lower after the nape has been called as a target, the shot misses.  <br />\nThe head can be chosen as a target to incapacitate by the aimer, with a regular roll as usual. If it is hit, the Titan’s head is blasted off with a crippling wound. It is still alive, but cannot eat, see, or hear until its head regenerates fully.  <br />\nIf a human is hit with a cannon, they take a crippling blunt wound on a limb of the aimer’s choice.</p>",
