        "difficult": false,
        "combat": false,
        "source": "The opposite of Your Duties",
        "description": "<h2 id=\"the-opposite-of-your-duties\">The <em>opposite</em> of Your Duties</h2>\n<p>Sometimes, you need a break on the job. When drinking, <strong>Roll + Body</strong>. On a 6 or lower, decrease Agility and Technique by one. On a 7-9, increase Heart by one, and decrease your choice of Agility or Technique by one. On a 10+, increase Heart by one.  <br />\nWhen sobering up, <strong>Roll + Duty</strong>. On a 7+, you lose the effects of inebriation. When someone is helping you, the helper should make the appropriate roll, then take the average. Add both rolls and divide by two, rounding down.  <br />\nWhen taking a night to rest, <strong>Roll + Heart</strong>. On a 10+, you regain all points of consciousness, and your minor wounds are healed. On a 7-9, you only regain all consciousness. On a 6 or lower, you cannot sleep. This roll is automatically failed if you have any major wounds, but does not apply to crippling wounds, so long as they’ve been treated if they’re cutting wounds, or amputated if they’re any other kind of wound.</p>",
