        "description": "<h3 id=\"titan-shifter-regeneration\"><em>Titan Shifter Regeneration</em></h3>\n<p>When wounded, a Titan form will heal at the same rate as a regular Titan, and they similarly can only be knocked out through slicing out their nape, or receiving a crippling head blow from a similar-sized opponent, which would result in the shifter being torn out of their Titan form.  <br />\nTitan Shifters outside of their Titan form will not heal quite as fast as Titans. They’re still affected by consciousness, but will heal minor wounds in a matter of minutes, at the GM’s discretion. When resting, Titan Shifters may <strong>Roll + Heart</strong> to turn a major wound into a minor wound, with the same rules as regularly healing a minor wound.  If they have a crippling wound anywhere on their body, they are unable to transform. Crippling wounds can only be healed on a Titan Shifter, and will be healed once the mission has ended, or they’ve had a full night to rest.  <br />\nWhen dismounting your Titan Form, <strong>Roll + Body</strong>. On a 7+, you manage to get out with no issue. On a 6 or lower, you are stuck inside, and immediately fail the first state of Absorption. When dismounting your Titan form, your consciousness is reduced to one, and you must wait for it to regenerate before you can transform again.</p>",
