        "key": "resist-final-absorption",
        "stat": "heart",
        "category": "Shifting",
        "difficult": false,
        "combat": false,
        "source": "Absorption",
        "description": "<h3 id=\"absorption\"><em>Absorption</em></h3>\n<p>Slowly, but surely, a human will be absorbed into the nape of their Titan. Humans within Mindless Titans are instantaneously absorbed, and can only be retrieved through eating a Titan Shifter. Within shifters, however, they are slowly absorbed over time. After a decent amount of time has passed, and you’re beginning to grow tired, <strong>Roll + Heart</strong>. On a 7-9, your limbs are completely fused with the Titan’s nape, and must be severed to cut you free. You are completely fine at this point other than that, however, and can continue as normal. Each subsequent roll of this, at the GM’s discretion, should apply a negative modifier of one, similar to the rules for dodging.  <br />\nOnce you’ve become completely exhausted and you’ve been in your Titan Form for hours, <strong>Roll + Heart</strong> after every action you take. On a 7-9, you fly into a maddened rage, and attack everything around you. On a 10+ you manage to hold on just a little longer. On a 6 or lower, you fly into a maddened rage, and you are completely fused into your nape. At this point, slicing your nape would only kill you, and the only way to salvage your Titan power is to have another Titan bite your nape off.</p>",
